  "worked_solution": "We're given that\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=u(x){y}_{1}(x)=ux.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating ${y}_{2}=ux$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{\u2032} & ={u}^{\u2032}x+u \\\\ {y}_{2}^{\u2033} & ={u}^{\u2033}x+2{u}^{\u2032}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}({u}^{\u2033}x+2{u}^{\u2032})-2x(x+1)({u}^{\u2032}x+u)+2(x+1)(ux) & =0 \\\\ {u}^{\u2033}{x}^{3}+2{u}^{\u2032}{x}^{2}-2{u}^{\u2032}{x}^{2}(x+1)-2ux(x+1)+2ux(x+1) & =0 \\\\ {u}^{\u2033}{x}^{3}+2{u}^{\u2032}{x}^{2}-2{u}^{\u2032}{x}^{3}-2{u}^{\u2032}{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {u}^{\u2033}{x}^{3}-2{u}^{\u2032}{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3}({u}^{\u2033}-2{u}^{\u2032}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${x}^{3}\\ne 0$ for $x>0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{\u2033}-2{u}^{\u2032}=0.\n$$",
